\section{Introduction}
Taikat (ISO 639-3 aos; Glottocode taik1255; also Daiget, Tajkat, Arso, Abrap) is a Border-family Papuan language spoken around Arso in Keerom Regency, Papua, Indonesia. Search results give conflicting speaker figures (about 500 around 2000, 600 in 1978, a community estimate of about 3,500), and note shift among younger people. No school materials, primers or curricula were found.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, Taikat language: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taikat_language}
\item ASJP word-list entry (Taikat 2): \url{https://asjp.clld.org/languages/TAIKAT_2}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Joshua Project people-group profile, Taikat in Indonesia (a mission-oriented demographic profile): \url{https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/15196}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Endangered Languages Project entry: \url{https://endangeredlanguages.com/lang/2783}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Only catalogue-level and word-list sources were found. A curriculum would require new documentation work with Taikat communities in Keerom Regency; no existing programme was found.
